Forge - AI model compiler for ARM64 

USAGE:  forge [OPTIONS] <model.onnx>


POSITIONALS:
  input TEXT REQUIRED         Input model file (.onnx) 

OPTIONS:
  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit 
          --version           Display program version information and exit 
  -o,     --output TEXT       Output file 
  -b,     --backend TEXT:{neon,sve,apu,vulkan} 
                              Backend: neon|sve|apu|vulkan 
          --verify-tensors    Print per-tensor metadata + FNV-1a hash (for validation) 

EXAMPLES: 
forge model.onnx Analyze with default backend 
forge model.onnx --backend=neon Use ARM NEON (SIMD) 
forge model.onnx --backend=sve Use ARM SVE/SVE2 
forge model.onnx --backend=apu Use MediaTek APU 
forge model.onnx --backend=vulkan Use Mali GPU 
forge model.onnx -o generated.c Save generated code 

SUPPORTED FORMATS: 
.onnx ONNX models (Opset 7 through 17+) 

EXIT CODES: 
0 Success 
1 Invalid model or parse error 
2 Unexpected runtime error 

